  "body": "Some locations sell themselves and Half Moon Bay is one of them. Two new freehold homes have arrived at 1&2/8 Indus Place, just a 5 minute walk from Half Moon Bay Marina in one of East Auckland's most desirable coastal pockets.\r\n\r\nDownstairs, the open-plan dining and living areas become the natural hub of each home, made for busy weeknights and relaxed weekends with family and friends. Flowing out to a deck that wraps around the side of the house, indoor-outdoor living becomes a part of everyday life, whether it's morning coffee, summer barbecues or an evening drink.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, where all four bedrooms are located, everyone has their own space. The master has a private ensuite and with 2 bathrooms and the luxury of a powder room, the morning rush is sorted. A study nook completes the upper level, a quiet spot for working from home or homework without giving up a bedroom.\r\n\r\nA private gate at the front of the home adds security and privacy, while a single external garage takes care of parking and storage, keeping the car and the clutter out of the living space.\r\n\r\nThen there's the location and this is the real drawcard. With the Marina just 5 minutes on foot, waterfront walks, weekend coffees and evenings by the water become part of your routine rather than a drive away. Shops, cafes and restaurants are close by and the Marina's ferry services make the commute to the city an easy option. It's a coastal lifestyle that suits families, professionals and anyone who wants to leave the car at home more often.\r\n\r\nFamilies are well placed too with the homes in zone for Pigeon Mountain Primary, Farm Cove Intermediate and Pakuranga College.\r\n\r\nBrand new, freehold and a short walk from the water. The vendor welcomes genuine enquiry.\r\n\r\nFind more properties you may like at www.teamvishrealestate.co.nz",
